WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.749 --> 00:00:08.389
Lee Byung-chul, the founder of Samsung, explained
that the Korean Hanja of the word, Samsung,

00:00:08.389 --> 00:00:09.800
means “Three Stars”.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.760
The stars signified something that was eternal,
while three was symbolic for “big, numerous

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.760
and powerful”.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.910
That is precisely the feeling you’ll get
when you take a tour of their headquarters

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.220
called the Samsung Digital City located in
Suwon, just thirty kilometres south of Seoul

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.840
- South Korea’s capital.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.359
In fact, the multinational tech giant has
several buildings and developments in other

00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:30.890
nearby cities like Yongin and Hwasung.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:35.039
Together, the space occupied by Samsung in
these three regions is referred to as Samsung

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:36.210
Digital Valley.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:40.579
Our tour of the city revealed to us a similar
work ethic like that of Silicon Valley, however,

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:44.860
the level of care afforded to employees in
the digital city is perhaps rivalled by no

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.850
other company, and the effect of Samsung’s
presence to the locals is also a highly positive

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.850
relationship.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.100
Welcome back to our channel!

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.880
If you haven’t already, make sure you hit
the subscribe button and ring that bell, so

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.590
you’re notified every time we upload a new
video!

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:03.410
Now, you probably know Samsung as one of the
most recognizable and top cellphone manufacturers.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:06.950
And over the years, they have proven to have
earned that status through many of their sleek

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.360
designs and innovations in the mobile phone
industry (go through several short clips of

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.360
Samsung Phone designs throughout this sentence).

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.693
While some of their products have just straight
up been the bomb (clip of Samsung Note 7 exploding

00:01:13.693 --> 00:01:14.693
0:27 to 0:28).

00:01:14.693 --> 00:01:15.693
However, Samsung is much more than that.

00:01:15.693 --> 00:01:19.479
Samsung electronics may be the largest information
technology and consumer electronics maker

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.120
by revenue, but other large affiliates exist
too.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:27.020
For instance, Samsung Heavy is the second
largest shipbuilding company, Samsung Engineering

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.610
and Samsung C&amp;T Corporation are two of the
largest construction companies worldwide,

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:35.650
while Samsung Life Insurance is the fourteenth
largest insurance company in the world.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:39.740
So you can understand when the office space
in Samsung’s Suwon headquarters alone covers

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.979
three hundred and ninety acres; almost four
times as large as the Vatican and similar

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:45.840
in area to Monaco.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.759
Samsung Digital City is located in Suwon,
which is the last completely walled city in

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:50.759
the country.

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:54.399
The wall is a UNESCO heritage site, and as
a tourist attraction, it is the other reason

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:58.549
besides the presence of Samsung in the city,
that draws so many foreigners to Suwon.

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:02.760
During the Korean war, Samsung facilities
in Seoul were so damaged that the Samsung

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.520
founder, Lee Byung-chul, had to move from
the capital city to Suwon in 1951.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:13.020
By 1969, the company would diversify its interests
so Samsung Electronics could be born and it’s

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.040
headquarters, naturally, was fixed within
the walls of the city that saved it from destruction.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.200
Eventually, with the growth of Samsung, the
arrival of other subsidiaries and departments,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.011
and the effect of the companies on the lives
and employment of people in the city, Samsung

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:29.590
Digital City has evolved to accommodate the
explosive economic metamorphosis.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:34.959
In fact, two other cities now also house semiconductor
factories for Samsung Electronics - Samsung

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:38.730
Nano City in Yongin, and Samsung Nano City
in Hwasung.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:42.650
Both cities are just a few kilometers from
Suwon and they reflect the fact that Samsung

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:46.760
really has spread out its roots in South Korea
like a tree from a little seed.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:51.950
Now, in Samsung Digital City, there are about
thirty-five thousand employees, four landmark

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:56.560
towers, over a hundred and thirty buildings
that include labs, offices, recreational facilities,

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.430
a guesthouse for visiting researchers, and
other facilities in the city that cater to

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.630
the large workforce.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.540
One of my favourites is the availability of
over a hundred and fifty teachers looking

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.800
after the children of some of the employees.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.190
Because if you have thirty-five thousand people
in a large area, unless those thirty-five

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.379
thousand people are these guys (clip of The
Unsullied from Game of Thrones), chances are

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:15.220
that they have children amongst them.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:18.910
That’s a very important step they’ve made,
just like the resting rooms for employees

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.970
with special treatments for pregnant women.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:25.140
Life is meant to be easy, and work is part
of life, so it’s great to see that you can

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.160
easily transport yourself to a hundred and
three different destinations on any of the

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.150
five hundred shuttle buses in Samsung Digital
City.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.900
But what does work look like in this place?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.050
Well, there's a MIMO Chamber where Galaxy
phones are tested.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:42.300
The MIMO, or Multiple-Input and Multiple-Output
Chamber is where radio links like 4G LTE are

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.330
experimented on.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:48.029
Speaking of connectivity and experimentation,
the most feared internet connectivity, 5G,

00:03:48.029 --> 00:03:50.410
has it's own testing space called 5G city.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:55.050
In 5G city, Samsung workers experiment on
how to get the technology up and running for

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:59.019
the things it would be useful for like the
internet of things or IoT.

00:03:59.019 --> 00:04:03.659
IoT will create interconnected objects that
will be able to exchange data wirelessly and

00:04:03.659 --> 00:04:08.530
do awesome stuff like; your fridge and smartwatch
conspiring to advise you from eating late

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.580
at night and save your life.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.690
What a diabolical and despicable technology!

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:14.769
(Chuckle)

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:19.910
There’s also the anechoic chamber which
works to get the best conditions for the audio

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.440
tests of Samsung electronics.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:27.360
It does this by absorbing both sound and electromagnetic
waves, thus eliminating every form of reverberation

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.610
or echo and simulating an infinitely large
room.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:32.160
The name “an-echoic” (emphasize both parts
separated by the hyphen in “an-echoic”)

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.810
is derived from the fact that the room lacks
any echo.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:39.210
And you wouldn’t believe the amount of work
that went into the sounds for Samsung electronics.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:43.190
Because there’s a whole team of music artists
and producers working daily in the company’s

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:47.310
Sound Lab to develop even the tiniest of sounds
that you get from a Samsung device.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:51.660
The voicing of Bixby - Samsung’s virtual
assistant, your chat notification, the sound

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:56.130
of your air conditioner turning off, the sounds
from your smart TV, name it!

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.291
These guys have got it covered (clip of people
in the Sound Lab).

00:04:58.291 --> 00:05:02.442
The Digital City also has the Samsung Innovation
Museum where you can time travel (clip of

00:05:02.442 --> 00:05:04.360
Loki disappearing with the Tesseract) through
the rich history of innovation at the company

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.670
since its inception in 1938.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:10.590
And there are also older objects from two
hundred and seventy years ago that will inspire

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:15.020
anyone looking at them as they basically tell
the story of human ingenuity.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.940
This is the kind of inspiring environment
that the employees work in, and there’s

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:19.940
more.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:24.310
Employees have access to free healthcare services
like flu shots, dental treatment, physicals,

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:25.970
and traditional acupuncture.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.842
It get's even more healthy as employees can
engage in a variety of sports with the availability

00:05:29.842 --> 00:05:35.080
of many sporting facilities like the ten basketball
courts, four badminton courts, two baseball

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.250
diamonds, three soccer fields and an Olympic-sized
swimming pool.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:44.000
There are also over six hundred and fifty
employee clubs where workers indulge in once-in-a-lifetime

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.170
fantasies like paragliding or regular hobbies
like photography.

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:52.180
There are also many events from rock concerts
or a string quartet that you’ll bump into

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:55.160
every now and then in the City’s many open
spaces.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:59.750
The most loved event is Family Day where the
entire Samsung Digital City gets turned into

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:04.380
a theme park and employees even ride around
in go-karts and have fun with their friends

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.380
and families.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.729
I’d be tempted to say that Family Day is
the ultimate inspiration, but that would be

00:06:09.729 --> 00:06:11.930
food, and Samsung knows this as well.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:16.470
That’s why they have a four thousand-seater
cafeteria with almost a hundred different

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:17.860
delicacies on its menu.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:21.970
The company serves over seventy-two thousand
meals over the course of breakfast, lunch,

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:22.970
and dinner.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:27.310
And the food is the biggest inspiration not
just because it fills the bellies of the employees,

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:32.080
it also fills the bellies of the locals living
around the towns of Suwon, Yongin, and Hwasung.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.850
You see, serving seventy-two thousand meals
every day creates a large demand for foodstuff

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:40.330
which the local farmers are more than willing
to supply.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:44.240
This is part of a long history of the company's
positive influence on the country.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.389
Take for instance, the fact that Samsung is
considered as the major driving force behind

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:52.340
the country's economic resurgence also called
the "Miracle of Han River".

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:56.849
Samsung and it's affiliate companies are responsible
for a fifth of South Korea's exports, and

00:06:56.849 --> 00:07:00.870
the company's revenues has been estimated
to be about seventeen percent of the country's

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.750
total GDP.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:07.400
Samsung C&amp;T has a major hand in South Urban
development, building over two hundred thousand

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.740
houses in the country since the eighties.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:13.819
The importance of the company's presence in
the country cannot be overstated but it can

00:07:13.819 --> 00:07:18.150
be summed in the way that a Washington Post
headline once put it, "In South Korea, the

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:20.020
Republic of Samsung".

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:24.009
But we all know it goes beyond the borders
of the "Land of the Morning Calm".

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:28.040
Samsung is immense, and we can see how their
attention to giving their workers the best

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.669
in their Digital City and Digital Valley has
driven innovation and a brilliant work ethic

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:36.030
that has helped them take over several sectors
of industry in the world.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:39.982
I personally like Samsung's Headquarters not
just because it's awesome, but also because

00:07:39.982 --> 00:07:43.639
any apple you'll see (picture of an apple)
here are healthy, and the windows here (picture

00:07:43.639 --> 00:07:45.740
of office windows) are transparent.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.710
What do you think of this Digital City?

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.700
Where would you prefer to work than here?

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.500
Also, do you think Tesla's new Starbase city
will give it a run for its money (pop-up of

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:54.500
our video on how Tesla builds rockets in a
week)?

